---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import SystemInterface from "../components/SystemInterface.astro";
import GrowthLoop from "../components/GrowthLoop.astro";
import AuditClose from "../components/AuditClose.astro";
import FAQ from "../components/FAQ.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Anchorline Systems | Systems that help good organizations grow"
  description="We build the systems that help good organizations grow. Strategy, intelligence, technology, and hands-on execution for established businesses and organizations."
>
  <section class="r-home-hero container">
    <div class="r-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">STRATEGY · INTELLIGENCE · TECHNOLOGY · EXECUTION</p>
      <h1>We build the systems that help good organizations grow.</h1>
      <p class="r-lede">
        Anchorline helps established businesses and organizations increase
        visibility, create real opportunities, and turn more of them into
        measurable results—through strategy, intelligence, technology, and
        hands-on execution.
      </p>
      <div class="r-actions">
        <CTA location="hero" /><a class="r-secondary" href="/growth-engine/"
          >See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="r-outcomes">
        <span>More<br /><b>Opportunities</b></span><span
          >Better<br /><b>Conversations</b></span
        ><span>Real<br /><b>Results</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <SystemInterface />
  </section>
  <div class="r-conviction container">
    <span class="mono">FOUNDER-LED. HANDS-ON. ACCOUNTABLE.</span><p>
      Built around your organization.<br class="r-mobile-only" /> Not a predetermined
      stack of tools.
    </p><a href="/approach/">Our approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <section class="r-section container r-split" id="why-connected">
    <div class="r-editorial" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE CHALLENGE</p><h2>
        Most growth problems aren’t really marketing problems.
      </h2><p>
        Leads go cold. Websites don’t convert. Marketing doesn’t talk to sales.
        Data exists but nobody knows what to do with it. Teams add more tools
        instead of fixing the system.
      </p><p class="r-emphasis">
        Growth breaks down when the pieces don’t work together.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="r-disconnected"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Disconnected tools, cold leads, low visibility and lost opportunities leave gaps in the growth system."
      data-reveal
    >
      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 390" aria-hidden="true"
        ><path d="M100 85H245V175H440M180 300V205H355V95M290 300H420"
        ></path></svg
      >
      <div class="r-fragment" data-depth="8">
        <span aria-hidden="true">◫</span><strong>Disconnected tools</strong
        ><small>No shared context</small>
      </div><div class="r-fragment" data-depth="-10">
        <span aria-hidden="true">◷</span><strong>Leads go cold</strong><small
          >No clear next step</small
        >
      </div><div class="r-fragment" data-depth="14">
        <span aria-hidden="true">◎</span><strong>Low visibility</strong><small
          >Good work goes unseen</small
        >
      </div><div class="r-fragment" data-depth="-6">
        <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span><strong>Lost opportunities</strong
        ><small>The handoff breaks down</small>
      </div>
      <span class="r-gap-label mono">THE GAPS ARE WHERE GROWTH GETS LOST.</span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="r-philosophy container" data-reveal>
    <div class="v-diagnosis-brief" aria-label="Illustrative growth diagnosis">
      <span class="mono">GROWTH DIAGNOSIS / EXAMPLE</span><strong
        >Where does the opportunity break down?</strong
      ><dl>
        <div><dt>Acquisition</dt><dd>The right audience</dd></div><div>
          <dt>Conversion</dt><dd>A clear next step</dd>
        </div><div><dt>Follow-up</dt><dd>Accountable ownership</dd></div>
      </dl><span class="v-diagnosis-foot"
        >OBSERVATION → PRIORITY → NEXT MOVE</span>
    </div>
    <p class="eyebrow">A DIFFERENT STARTING POINT</p><h2>
      We don’t start with tools.<br />We start with where growth is actually
      breaking down.
    </h2><p>
      Then we connect the strategy, people, technology, and execution required
      to move it forward.
    </p><a class="text-link" href="/approach/"
      >How we approach the work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    >
  </section>
  <section class="r-section r-engine-section" id="systems">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="r-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">THE ANCHORLINE GROWTH ENGINE</p><h2>
            Not more pieces.<br />A system that connects them.
          </h2>
        </div><p>
          The Growth Engine is our flagship commercial system. Configured around
          your organization, it brings the work of growth into one connected
          process.
        </p>
      </div>
      <GrowthLoop />
      <div class="r-engine-link">
        <p>
          Strategy sets the direction. Intelligence improves the decisions.
          Execution makes them real.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/growth-engine/"
          >Inside the Growth Engine <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container" id="pathways">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">DIFFERENT MARKETS. THE SAME SYSTEMS THINKING.</p><h2>
          Configured for how<br />your customers buy.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div><div class="pathway-composition">
      <article class="market-path market-b2b">
        <div class="path-top">
          <span class="mono">01 / B2B GROWTH</span><div
            class="mini-pipeline"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
          </div>
        </div><h3>
          Find the right companies.<br />Start the right conversations.
        </h3><p>
          For established B2B and service organizations connecting buyer
          intelligence, outbound acquisition, qualified conversations, and
          conversion.
        </p><ul class="inline-list">
          <li>Buyer intelligence</li><li>Outbound acquisition</li><li>
            Pipeline & conversion
          </li>
        </ul><a href="/growth-engine/b2b/" class="text-link"
          >Explore B2B Growth <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article><article class="market-path market-local">
        <div class="path-top">
          <span class="mono">02 / LOCAL GROWTH</span><div
            class="mini-local"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <i></i><i></i><b></b>
          </div>
        </div><h3>Get found.<br />Build trust. Grow your business.</h3><p>
          For local businesses connecting websites, search visibility,
          reputation, paid demand, lead capture, and timely follow-up.
        </p><ul class="inline-list">
          <li>Local visibility</li><li>Website & reputation</li><li>
            Leads & follow-up
          </li>
        </ul><a href="/growth-engine/local/" class="text-link"
          >Explore Local Growth <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section work-section">
    <div class="container work-composition">
      <div class="work-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHAT THE WORK LOOKS LIKE</p><h2>
          Useful intelligence.<br />Tangible execution.
        </h2><p>
          Research should change a decision. An asset should help a
          conversation. A website should make the next step easier.
        </p><p>
          Anchorline’s work can include buyer research, prioritized audits,
          personalized prospect assets, conversion improvements, and operating
          reports—selected for your growth configuration.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/growth-engine/#outputs"
          >Explore the operating outputs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div><div class="dossier-stage">
        <article
          class="dossier dossier-back"
          aria-hidden="true"
          data-depth="14"
        >
          <div class="mono">ACCOUNT INTELLIGENCE</div><h3>
            Context before<br />contact.
          </h3><div class="doc-line"></div><div class="doc-line short">
          </div><div class="doc-grid">
            <span>FIT</span><span>SIGNALS</span><span>BUYERS</span><span
              >NEXT STEP</span
            >
          </div>
        </article><article class="dossier dossier-front" data-depth="-12">
          <div class="dossier-top mono">
            <span>GROWTH AUDIT</span><span>EXAMPLE FORMAT</span>
          </div><h3>Three priorities.<br />A clearer next move.</h3><ol>
            <li>
              <span>01</span><div>
                <strong>Attract</strong><p>
                  Where the right customers may be missing you.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li><li>
              <span>02</span><div>
                <strong>Convert</strong><p>
                  Where interest meets avoidable friction.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li><li>
              <span>03</span><div>
                <strong>Follow up</strong><p>
                  Where a useful conversation can lose momentum.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol><p class="artifact-note">
            Illustrative deliverable structure, not a client result.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container v-operator">
    <figure class="v-operator-portrait">
      <img
        src="/kris-mcfadden.webp"
        alt="Kris McFadden, founder and CEO of Anchorline Systems"
        width="600"
        height="601"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      /><figcaption><strong>Kris McFadden</strong>Founder & CEO</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">BUILT. OPERATED. ACCOUNTABLE.</p><h2>
        Built by an operator.<br /><span class="muted-heading"
          >Accountable to the work.</span
        >
      </h2>
    </div><div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="large-copy">The system matters. So does who operates it.</p><p>
        Anchorline brings intelligence, digital execution, and operating
        discipline into one engagement. The scope defines what gets built, what
        gets operated, and how progress is reviewed.
      </p><p>
        Led by founder and CEO Kris McFadden, Anchorline brings organizational
        leadership, systems thinking, judgment, and hands-on execution to the
        work.
      </p><a class="text-link" href="/about/"
        >Meet Anchorline <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section process-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">HOW AN ENGAGEMENT TAKES SHAPE</p><h2>
            Start with clarity.<br />Build what matters.
          </h2>
        </div>
      </div><ol class="engagement-steps">
        <li>
          <span class="mono">01</span><h3>Audit</h3><p>
            Identify three high-priority growth opportunities.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">02</span><h3>Configure</h3><p>
            Agree on the right Growth Engine scope and responsibilities.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>
            Connect the assets, workflows, and conversion infrastructure.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">04</span><h3>Operate & improve</h3><p>
            Review signals, coordinate action, and refine the system.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container faq-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">BEFORE WE TALK</p><h2>A few useful answers.</h2>
    </div><FAQ
      items={[
        [
          "Is Anchorline a software subscription or a growth partner?",
          "The Growth Engine is a configured growth engagement—not a self-service software subscription. Anchorline builds and operates the agreed system; capabilities and responsibilities are scoped to the business.",
        ],
        [
          "Do we have to replace our existing tools?",
          "Not by default. The audit looks for what is working, where the gaps are, and what should connect. Existing assets and systems should be reused when they support the agreed outcome.",
        ],
        [
          "Does the audit include implementation?",
          "No. The no-cost, qualification-based audit identifies three priorities, supporting observations, a recommended configuration, and a next step. Implementation is a separately scoped engagement.",
        ],
        [
          "Can local businesses use the same Growth Engine?",
          "Yes. Local Growth is a primary configuration of the same engine, focused on how nearby customers find, evaluate, contact, and buy from a business.",
        ],
        [
          "Do you guarantee leads or revenue?",
          "No. Recommendations and delivery are grounded in the agreed scope and available evidence. Results depend on factors including market conditions, the offer, execution, and the sales process.",
        ],
      ]}
    />
  </section>
  <AuditClose />
</Site>
